Z||000010||Raydar||12-12-1999||12:39 PM||||Marvel Mystery Oil? Never heard of adding that to the ATF. I have heard of pouring brake fluid into a poorly performing A.T. Supposedly causes the seals to swell, and restores hydraulic pressure. (I've never tried it. My A.T. failures have been of the "broken parts" category. Long time ago. Ford. Won't elaborate.) I find this theory interesting, since people are now using ATF in place of DOT-3 in their clutch hydraulics, for the same reason. Seems like two conflicting theories, here. Anyone? ||||reg||1
Z||000011||mutfish||12-14-1999||08:20 PM||||If somebody claims to have fixed their broken automatic trans by switching from atf to brake fluid I'm leavin'.....||||reg||1
